-- title:
--   Separatedness of a scheme representing relative Pic⁰
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, let $C$ be a scheme and let $c \colon C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$, that is, a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ whose composite with $c$ is the identity. Assume the hypothesis $h\mathfrak{F}$: for every $m_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ there is finite map data $\mathfrak{F}$ for $(c,\varepsilon)$ with $m_0 \le \mathfrak{F}.m$, where such data consist of two affine opens $U, V$ covering $C$ with $U$ the locus of points outside the range of $\varepsilon$, sections $f \in \Gamma(C,U)$, $g \in \Gamma(C,V)$ whose restrictions to $U \cap V$ are mutually inverse and cut out $U \cap V$ as the basic open set of either, finiteness of $\Gamma(C,U)$ over $R[T]$ via $f$ and of $\Gamma(C,V)$ over $R[T]$ via $g$, and the requirement that for every local $R$-algebra $S$ and every $s \in S$ the quotient $S \otimes_R \Gamma(C,U)$ by the ideal generated by $1 \otimes f - s \otimes 1$ be finite and free over $S$ of rank $\mathfrak{F}.m$. Let $D$ be a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation for $c$, i.e. a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase} \colon D.P \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and a section $D.\mathrm{zeroSection}$ of it, and let $h$ witness that $D$ represents the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles singled out by the condition `algEquivZeroCut`, namely that a rigidified line bundle $M$ on $C \times_R T$ satisfies `FibrewiseAlgEquivZero`: for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every $s \colon \operatorname{Spec} k \to T$, the pullback of $M.L$ to the fibre of $C \times_R T$ at $s$ satisfies the predicate `IsAlgEquivZero`. Thus $h$ provides a Poincaré rigidified bundle on $C \times_R D.P$ satisfying this condition, the universal property that every rigidified bundle satisfying the condition over a base $t \colon T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ is the pullback of the Poincaré bundle along a unique morphism $T \to D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$, and an isomorphism of the pullback along the zero section with the unit bundle. Assume finally that $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is locally of finite type. Then $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is separated.
--
--   This is the separatedness half of the basic geometric properties of the Jacobian of a pointed smooth proper curve, obtained from the representability of relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ rather than from a construction: the diagonal locus in $D.P \times_R D.P$ is identified with the locus where a rigidified bundle becomes fibrewise trivial, which is closed by [`AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.isClosed_setOf_exists_fibreModule_iso_unit`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.isClosed_setOf_exists_fibreModule_iso_unit). It feeds into [`AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.isProper_and_geometricallyConnected_of_representsRelSubPic_algEquivZeroCut_of_finiteMapData`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard.isProper_and_geometricallyConnected_of_representsRelSubPic_algEquivZeroCut_of_finiteMapData), where properness and geometric connectedness of the representing scheme are assembled.
